- So tell everybody

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:04.530
about what this is about

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:05.940
if they haven't seen the first season.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:09.720
- Your Honor is about
a superior court judge

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:12.990
who is a very honorable man

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:17.910
and he has a, a teenage son
who gets into a car accident,

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.460
leaves the scene of the
accident, which is a crime

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:21.390
- Makes a poor decision.

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:22.470
- Yes.

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:25.380
And I come home, he tells
me about it and I say

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:26.970
you gotta do the right thing.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:30.270
I take him to the police
station to turn him in

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:33.750
and I discover that the
boy who was actually

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.440
killed in this accident
is the son of a mob boss.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:42.330
And I know with every
being in my, in my soul

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.820
that that man would kill my son.

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:49.590
Yeah. So on that moment
of, of decision, I decide

00:09:49.590 --> 00:09:53.880
not to turn him into the
police to protect him and

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:57.300
with the conceit of if I did,
he would, he would be dead.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:01.380
So everything starts to
spiral out of control.

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:03.114
And that's the first season. Now,

00:10:03.114 --> 00:10:04.110
- Yeah

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:05.042
- we're in the second season.

00:10:05.042 --> 00:10:06.360
- Yeah.
- What happens?

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:10.050
It ended tragically, I'll just
say that in the first season,

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:11.610
second season, I wanted to

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:16.590
explore what would that feel
like if all, if that loss

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:20.310
of a child, God forbid,
what would that feel like?

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:22.860
And so Showtime was willing to go in

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:24.599
and explore that.

00:10:24.599 --> 00:10:27.054
- Yeah.
- Of grief and despair and

00:10:27.054 --> 00:10:27.887
- That's real.

00:10:27.887 --> 00:10:28.720
- It's real.

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:30.300
And is there a life after that?

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:33.360
And so, but I will say that this season

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:36.030
with all the excitement and tension,

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.550
it ends up in a different
way than the first,

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:40.110
first ended in tragedy.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:41.670
This ends hopefully.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:42.503
- Hopeful?

00:10:42.503 --> 00:10:43.336
- Yeah.

00:10:43.336 --> 00:10:44.169
- Is that hard?

00:10:44.169 --> 00:10:45.990
Like I, I know you're an
actor, you're all acting.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:46.823
I get it.

00:10:46.823 --> 00:10:50.580
But is it hard when you
are a parent to do scenes

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.740
like that when you have to
go to that place of like

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:55.669
what if I lost my, I don't,
that would be very hard.

00:10:55.669 --> 00:11:00.310
- I, I did a scene on Breaking
Bad where I was watching

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:05.280
a woman die in the second season and

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:06.450
being prepared for that.

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:10.350
And all of a sudden her
face left and the face

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:13.320
of my real daughter showed
up and I was watching

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:14.880
my real daughter die.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:15.960
- Yeah.
- In front of me.

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:17.370
And it choked me.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:18.930
I even get a little choked up.

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:20.040
- I know. I'm like, I'm tearing up.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:20.940
Don't do that. What am I gonna

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:21.773
- Do about it now.

00:11:21.773 --> 00:11:23.070
Yeah.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:25.800
- And, and it, it, for about two

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:30.030
or three seconds I saw my
daughter's face choked me up

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:31.050
and then that went away

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:32.963
and Kristen Ritter's face came back and

00:11:32.963 --> 00:11:33.796
- Yeah.

00:11:33.796 --> 00:11:34.629
- And there she was.

00:11:34.629 --> 00:11:36.720
And, and it was like, oh my God.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:40.560
And it is, it is emotional
risk that actors go through.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:42.840
We have to put ourselves in a position

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:46.254
of vulnerability for that to
possibly happen because you're

00:11:46.254 --> 00:11:48.776
you're willing to go
into the unknown really.

00:11:48.776 --> 00:11:50.513
Yeah. Yeah.

